.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ECCE-QM, B3LYP/6-31G*, optimisation and frequencies, orbitals localised. This calculation shows a carbon-carbon triple bond: in the MOs panel, field type Localised MO, one sigma C1-C2 and two pi C1-C2 orbitals. The optimised C-C distance is 1.205 Å, shorter than in ethene, and the totally symmetric C-C stretch is at 2085.58 cm-1 (IR inactive), higher than in ethene.
